feat 1.0

# SPEC-RT-003 (AMENDED copy, founder ruling c7af7871 of 2026-11-09) — the harness and faults
# (ADR-0023 D3): a fault the case declares is armed as a precondition, consumed by the named
# operation, checked for consumption, and disarmed by the next reset; a fault the binding cannot
# produce, or cannot produce with the count the case writes, stops the case before it has any
# effect. DRAFT: status draft; this file replaces harness-faults.feat when the founder agrees the
# amendment.
#
# WHAT CHANGED versus harness-faults.feat (and nothing else):
#  1. Catalog shape: an operation maps each fault to the counts it DECLARES, ["once", "times",
#     "reset"] in any subset (`times` covers every n). The earlier shape, an array of fault
#     names, is still accepted and means all three counts.
#  2. The hold-only mechanism (stub option holdOnly, the special case for Connection) is gone:
#     a hold-only fault is simply one that declares ["reset"].
#  3. Preflight refuses a count the fault does not declare: FAULT_UNSUPPORTED, same code, same
#     moment, detail names the declared counts.
#  4. Stub and fixtures: options.faults has the new shape and options.holdOnly is removed;
#     fault.config.json declares AccessDenied as ["reset"] and Connection.Timeout as ["reset"];
#     a new fixture fault-legacy.config.json keeps the array shape.
#  5. Scenarios: "a transport fault that is not until reset ..." is replaced by "a count the fault
#     does not declare ..." (same expectation, new reason text); two scenarios are added (a
#     non-transport fault declaring only reset; the legacy array shape).
# Unchanged: the contract file, every other scenario, the arm/consume/fire order, FAULT_NOT_CONSUMED. Builds only after the `fault` amendment of
# SPEC-CORE-001 (parse) and SPEC-RT-002 (the check that runs first) are agreed.
#
# Driven through the same probe as SPEC-RT-002 (`RunHarnessCase { config, cases }`). Its stub
# service adapter (fixtures/harness/stub.mjs) is extended: options.faults is its catalog
# ({ AppendToStream: { NotLeader: [once, times, reset], WrongExpectedVersion: [once, times, reset],
# AccessDenied: [reset] }, Connection: { Timeout: [reset] } }),
# options.observed decides whether it implements firedFaults(), and `fault()` absent from the
# stub when options.faults is absent. The response stub's Ping { appends: n } makes n calls of
# AppendToStream on the store stub, each answering ok or the armed fault's name. The probe adds
# to the calls string: arm:<service>=<Operation>/<Fault>/<times|reset> when fault() is called,
# consume:<service>=<Operation>:<ok|Fault> for each system call of an operation, and
# fired:<service> when firedFaults() is called; `armedDetail` renders the last arm's detail as
# key=value pairs; `violationCodes` is the comma-joined violation codes of a failed case.
# Fixture configs (all: response stub `response` with command Ping, service `store` strong, no
# setClock): fault.config.json (catalog above, observed), fault-unobserved.config.json (same,
# no firedFaults), no-fault.config.json (no fault method), fault-legacy.config.json (catalog in the
# earlier array shape: { AppendToStream: [NotLeader] }).
#
# What the order pins: preflight -> reset -> seeds -> given executes -> arm -> startCapture ->
# trigger -> stopCapture -> firedFaults -> diff. Executes run before arming, so setup that calls
# the faulted operation is never hit; arming is before the window, so it is never a capture.

spec SPEC-RT-003 "Harness: fault arming, consumption and refusal"
context Toolchain
aggregate Runtime
type infrastructure
status draft

construct:
  handler at packages/feat-runtime/src/harness.ts
  touches packages/feat-runtime/**
  touches packages/feat-types/**
  needs SPEC-RT-002
  needs SPEC-CORE-001
  Types (feat-types): HarnessCase.given.faults?: Fault[] (the IR shape); FaultCatalog =
  Record<string, readonly string[] | Record<string, readonly FaultCount[]>> with FaultCount =
  "once" | "times" | "reset"; FaultArm, FaultFiring; on FeatServiceAdapter `readonly faults?: FaultCatalog`, `fault?(arm: FaultArm)` and
  `firedFaults?(): Promise<FaultFiring[]>`.
  Preflight, in the same first step as SPEC-RT-002's checks and before any adapter call: for each
  fault of the case, the named service's adapter must have fault() and list the operation and the
  fault under it, and the count the case writes (once, times n, until reset) must be among the
  counts that fault declares (an array-shaped entry declares all three); otherwise throw
  HarnessConfigurationError FAULT_UNSUPPORTED with service and a detail that lists the adapter's
  catalog, or names the declared counts, or says "no fault()".
  Arm each fault in written order, after the given executes and before startCapture:
  fault({ operation, fault, detail, times }). After stopCapture, for each service that was armed and
  has firedFaults(), call it once: a fault armed times n must have fired n times and one armed until
  reset at least once, else add the violation FAULT_NOT_CONSUMED naming service, operation, fault,
  expected and actual. A service without firedFaults() is not checked.
  Adapter obligation, asserted by the adapter kit (not here): reset() disarms every fault.

enforce:
  check that every fault of the case is offered by its service's adapter before any adapter call
  rejects FAULT_UNSUPPORTED when a fault names an operation or a fault the adapter does not offer, an adapter with no fault method, or a count the fault does not declare
  arm the faults in written order after the given executes and before the capture window opens
  consume a once fault on the next call, a times n fault on the next n, an until reset fault on every call of the case
  fail the case with FAULT_NOT_CONSUMED when an observed fault fired fewer times than armed
  leave an adapter that cannot see consumption unchecked

contract:
  input RunInput
  response RunResult
  error HarnessError

scenario "faults are armed after the seeds and the given executes and before the capture window":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { seeds: [ { service: "store", records: [ { type: "Seeded", values: { n: 1 } } ] } ], executes: [ { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 1 } } ], faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 1 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 1 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "passed", calls: "reset:store seed:store execute:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:ok arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/1 start:store invoke:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader stop:store fired:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "once is the next call only":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 1 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 2 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "passed", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/1 start:store invoke:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader consume:store=AppendToStream:ok stop:store fired:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "times n is the next n calls":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 2 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 3 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "passed", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/2 start:store invoke:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader consume:store=AppendToStream:ok stop:store fired:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "until reset is every call of the case":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: "reset" } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 3 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "passed", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/reset start:store invoke:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader stop:store fired:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "several faults are armed in written order and the detail reaches the adapter":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "WrongExpectedVersion", detail: { stream: "orders" }, times: 1 }, { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 1 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 2 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "passed", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/WrongExpectedVersion/1 arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/1 start:store invoke:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:WrongExpectedVersion consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader stop:store fired:store", armedDetail: "stream=orders" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "reset disarms, so a fault never leaks into the next case":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: "reset" } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 1 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
      { anchor: "c2", name: "c2", when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 1 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "passed", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/reset start:store invoke:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader stop:store fired:store reset:store start:store invoke:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:ok stop:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "an armed fault the system never consumed fails the case":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 1 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 0 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "failed", violationCodes: "FAULT_NOT_CONSUMED", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/1 start:store invoke:Ping stop:store fired:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "times n consumed fewer than n times fails the case":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 3 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 2 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "failed", violationCodes: "FAULT_NOT_CONSUMED", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/3 start:store invoke:Ping consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader consume:store=AppendToStream:NotLeader stop:store fired:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "until reset never consumed fails the case":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: "reset" } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 0 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "failed", violationCodes: "FAULT_NOT_CONSUMED", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/reset start:store invoke:Ping stop:store fired:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "an adapter that cannot see consumption is exempt":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault-unobserved.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 1 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 0 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict success:
    response OK RunResult { outcome: "passed", calls: "reset:store arm:store=AppendToStream/NotLeader/1 start:store invoke:Ping stop:store" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "an operation the adapter does not offer is refused before any effect":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { executes: [ { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 1 } } ], faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "DeleteStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 1 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 1 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict rejection FAULT_UNSUPPORTED:
    response ERR HarnessError { code: "FAULT_UNSUPPORTED", calls: "", service: "store", detail: matching "AppendToStream" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a fault name the adapter does not offer is refused before any effect":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "Gremlins", times: 1 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 1 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict rejection FAULT_UNSUPPORTED:
    response ERR HarnessError { code: "FAULT_UNSUPPORTED", calls: "", service: "store", detail: matching "NotLeader" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "an adapter with no fault method is refused before any effect":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
    config: "packages/feat-runtime/fixtures/harness/no-fault.config.json"
    cases: [
      { anchor: "c1", name: "c1", given: { faults: [ { service: "store", operation: "AppendToStream", fault: "NotLeader", times: 1 } ] }, when: { command: "Ping", payload: { appends: 1 } }, prediction: { type: "success", services: { store: { ordering: "ordered", records: [] } } } }
    ]
  }
  predict rejection FAULT_UNSUPPORTED:
    response ERR HarnessError { code: "FAULT_UNSUPPORTED", calls: "", service: "store", detail: matching "fault" }
    filesystem has []

scenario "a count the fault does not declare is refused before any effect":
  when: RunHarnessCase {
